%% Figure 4.9 – State Machine Diagram: contribution.status (Contribution / reservation) + RowAllocation «planned» · v3.2 · 05/11/2026 · Register v1.4
%% Same content as CrabShare_State_Machines.drawio, page "contribution.status" (generated by gen-state.js, do not edit by hand).
%% «planned» = Register v1.4, not in code (class planned, grey dashed) · (not written by code) = CHECK value never written (class notwritten, orange dashed).
%% Labels are short (trigger [guard] / effect); the full label of each transition is in the %% line under it.
%% Design decisions of 05/11/2026 applied here were confirmed by the lead.
stateDiagram-v2
  state RowAllocation {
    state "Held «planned»" as Held
    state "Allocated «planned»" as Allocated
    state "Released «planned»" as Released
    [*] --> Held
    Held --> Allocated : «planned» contribution Confirmed · UC12
    %% «planned» contribution Confirmed / the row belongs to this investor · UC12
    Held --> Released : «planned» contribution Expired · UC10
    %% «planned» contribution Expired (timeout or cancel) / row free again · UC10
    Allocated --> Released : «planned» batch not opened / refund created · UC10
    %% «planned» batch not opened (funding close job) / contribution refund created · UC10
    Allocated --> [*] : «planned» batch Closed
    Released --> [*]
  }
  [*] --> Reserved : / reserve · UC10, UC11
  %% / created by reserve (Investor): expires_at = min(+30 min, funding deadline) · UC10, UC11 «planned» hold the picked box rows (RowAllocation Held)
  Reserved --> Confirmed : payment webhook [amount matches] / confirmed_at · UC12
  %% payment webhook [request Pending, amount matches, before expiry] / confirmed_at · UC12 «planned» rows Allocated
  Reserved --> Expired : after(expires_at) / QR Expired · UC10
  %% after(expires_at) or funding close (job) / QR Expired, void unsigned contract · UC10 «planned» rows Released
  Reserved --> Expired : cancel [not paid] · UC10
  %% cancel (Investor) [not paid] / QR Cancelled, void unsigned contract · UC10 «planned» rows Released
  Confirmed --> Refunded : refund Succeeded [batch Cancelled] / refunded_at · UC40
  %% Refund instruction Succeeded [batch Cancelled, amount = contribution] / refunded_at · UC40 «planned» also when the batch does not open for a low pre-order ratio; rows Released
  Confirmed --> [*] : batch Closed · UC39
  %% batch Closed (capital returned through the settlement line) · UC39
  Expired --> [*]
  Refunded --> [*]
  note right of RowAllocation
    RowAllocation is a separate «planned» state machine drawn on the same page - one RowAllocation per picked box row, following its contribution
    Held is «planned» (Register v1.4, not in code)
    Allocated is «planned» (Register v1.4, not in code)
    Released is «planned» (Register v1.4, not in code)
    «planned» Held → Allocated - contribution Confirmed / the row belongs to this investor
    «planned» Held → Released - contribution Expired (timeout or cancel) / row free again
    «planned» Allocated → Released - batch not opened (funding close job) / contribution refund created
    «planned» Allocated → end - batch Closed
  end note
  note right of Reserved
    «planned» on start → Reserved - hold the picked box rows (RowAllocation Held)
    «planned» precondition of start → Reserved - the picked box rows are free, amount = Σ (boxes in each row × Standard Cost per box), the minimum is one row's capital (the admin minimum contribution stays as a floor for a row's capital)
    «planned» on Reserved → Confirmed - rows Allocated
    «planned» on Reserved → Expired - rows Released
    «planned» RowAllocation (status Held, Allocated, Released) - a BoxRow belongs to the batch (its boxes grouped by physical_slot.row_code), each picked row is Held during the 30-minute reservation, Allocated when the contribution is Confirmed (a confirmed row belongs to exactly one investor, at most one active allocation per row) and Released when the contribution expires or is refunded. No table yet.
  end note
  note right of Confirmed
    «planned» on Confirmed → Refunded - also when the batch does not open for a low pre-order ratio, rows Released
  end note
  %% Created by reserve (Investor) only if: eKYC Verified, risk disclosure acknowledged, batch Funding and window open, min_contribution ≤ amount ≤ remaining capital, no other active hold in the batch; «planned» the picked box rows are free; amount = Σ (boxes in each row × Standard Cost per box); the minimum is one row's capital (the admin minimum contribution stays as a floor for a row's capital) (UC10, UC11).
  %% Capital close snapshots Confirmed contributions into capital_share (trigger trg_capital_share_immutable); the row itself stays Confirmed. Investors pay in full once before the batch opens, no instalments (Register v1.4) — as on develop.
  %% A webhook arriving after Expired is booked as LatePayment with an automatic Refund instruction (TL-10). Cancel = expire now (the CHECK has no Cancelled value).
  %% «planned» RowAllocation (status Held, Allocated, Released): a BoxRow belongs to the batch (its boxes grouped by physical_slot.row_code); each picked row is Held during the 30-minute reservation, Allocated when the contribution is Confirmed (a confirmed row belongs to exactly one investor; at most one active allocation per row) and Released when the contribution expires or is refunded. No table yet.
  classDef planned stroke-dasharray:5 5,stroke:#64748b,color:#64748b,fill:#f8fafc
  classDef notwritten stroke-dasharray:5 5,stroke:#9a3412,fill:#f1f5f9
  classDef terminal fill:#f1f5f9,stroke:#64748b
  class Held, Allocated, Released planned
  class Expired, Refunded terminal
